      {
        "heading": "The short version",
        "text": "Peyton Charles Paul Gray (born June 2, 1995) is an American professional baseball pitcher for the Texas Rangers of Major League Baseball (MLB). He made his MLB debut in 2026."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Lately",
        "text": "On January 21, 2025, Gray signed with the Texas Rangers organization. He split the 2025 season between the Frisco RoughRiders of the Double–A Texas League and the Round Rock Express of the Triple-A Pacific Coast League, going a combined 8–6 with a 3.58 ERA with 89 strikeouts over 73 innings. On April 23, 2026, Texas selected Gray's contract and promoted him to the major league roster for the first time. On May 30, Gray earned his first career win, recording two strikeouts across a scoreless inning of relief against the Kansas City Royals."
      }
